# Temporary Root Instruction Override

This file is an example. Copy it to `AGENTS.override.md` only when the root
instructions must be replaced temporarily. Because an override replaces
`AGENTS.md` at the same directory level, restate every project rule that must
remain active.

- Read `docs/agent/INDEX.md` before non-trivial work.
- Preserve user-owned changes and keep work scoped to the request.
- Do not modify database migrations during this task.
- Run targeted tests only unless broader verification is explicitly requested.
- Present a patch plan before editing authentication or authorization code.
- Report changed files, commands run, and remaining risks.
- After AI edits, before responding or handing off, append a concise summary to `change_logs/YYYY-MM-DD.md` using the local date. Create it as needed; reuse that day's file and preserve earlier entries. Include changes, key paths, and checks/pending work; omit secrets and private data. Read-only tasks need no entry.
